The variable hx represents the high 32 bits of the IEEE 754 representation of our input value after normalization.

In IEEE 754 double-precision format:
- The sign bit is the most significant bit
- The next 11 bits are the exponent
- The remaining 52 bits are the mantissa (with an implicit leading 1)

The high 32 bits (hx) would contain:
- The sign bit (1 bit)
- The exponent bits (11 bits)
- The top 20 bits of the mantissa

